<title>ITALY: Market turbulence if EMU delayed - Italy bank group.</title>
<headline>Market turbulence if EMU delayed - Italy bank group.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A delay to European economic and monetary union (EMU) would cause &quot;very serious turbulence&quot; in the financial markets, the head of the Italian banking association Abi said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;A delay would cause problems for everyone,&quot; Tancredi Bianchi told a the Senate budget commission.</p>
<p>He said it would not only prevent a fall in Italian interest rates, &quot;but could create problems for exchange rates and on the monetary policy of all countries (involved)&quot;.</p>
<p>The single European currency is due to be launched in 1999 but doubts over the timetable have arisen, with France on Monday asking for more time to study a budget stability pact which is designed to enforce fiscal restraint in EMU member states.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
